# Testing

## High-ROI Strategy

Only test code that is complex, critical, or prone to breaking.

## What TO Test

- Complex Cubits/BLoCs with multi-step logic, data transformations, or conditional flows.
- Core business logic classes with validation or calculation.

## What NOT to Test

- UI / widget tests (brittle, low ROI unless mission-critical reusable widget).
- Generated code (freezed, retrofit, injectable guarantee correctness).
- Simple passthrough repositories (`api.getUser(id)` → return).

## Tools

- `bloc_test` for Cubit state emission assertions.
- `mocktail` for mocking dependencies.

## Pattern

```dart
class MockAuthService extends Mock implements AuthService {}

blocTest<AuthCubit, AuthState>(
  'emits [loading, success] on login',
  build: () {
    when(() => mockAuth.login(any(), any())).thenAnswer((_) async => fakeUser);
    return AuthCubit(mockAuth);
  },
  act: (cubit) => cubit.login('test@email.com', 'pass'),
  expect: () => [const AuthState.loading(), AuthState.success(fakeUser)],
);
```
